# The flight computer (domains/avionics). It sits between the TX15 and ArduPilot. The TX15
# talks to it on a serial line (UART), in the CRSF protocol of ExpressLRS, not as a USB game
# controller (HID). The telemetry of ArduPilot goes the other way on the same line, and the
# ground station gets its telemetry from there. The tests run with no window: a simulated
# TX15 on the line, the flight computer, and an autopilot that reports its state. See
# domains/avionics/computer/tests/acceptance.rs.

Section: The flight computer
  The flight computer is a small computer that stands between the [[TX15]] and [[ArduPilot]].
  In the simulator it takes the place of the receiver and of the wiring in the plane. The TX15
  sends the sticks and switches down a serial line. The flight computer turns them into the
  radio channels that ArduPilot reads.

  The flight computer also sends the telemetry of ArduPilot back to the TX15 on the same line.
  The TX15 shows the flight mode, the battery and the bank on its screen. It also passes the
  [[MAVLink]] telemetry on to the ground station. The ground station gets no telemetry from
  any other place. The commands of the ground station go the same way in the other direction.

  Start the simulator with `--flight-computer PORT`. The simulator then ignores the USB
  controller. Only the serial line moves the plane.

Vocabulary:
  State: the TX15 is connected | not connected
    Set: connect the TX15 to the flight computer, or unplug it
    Shows: connected: the TX15 sends its channels down the serial line 150 times a second
  State: the TX15 roll stick is -100..100 %
    Set: move the roll stick of the TX15 to {value}
  State: the TX15 pitch stick is -100..100 %
    Set: move the pitch stick of the TX15 to {value}
  State: the TX15 throttle stick is 0..100 %
    Set: move the throttle stick of the TX15 to {value}
  State: the TX15 arm switch is off | on
    Set: put the arm switch of the TX15 {value}
  State: the roll channel is 800..2200 us
    Shows: {value}: the autopilot reads this pulse width on the roll channel
  State: the pitch channel is 800..2200 us
    Shows: {value}: the autopilot reads this pulse width on the pitch channel
  State: the throttle channel is 800..2200 us
    Shows: {value}: the autopilot reads this pulse width on the throttle channel
  State: the arm channel is 800..2200 us
    Shows: {value}: the autopilot reads this pulse width on the channel of the arm switch
  State: the corrupted frames are 0..100 %
    Set: let this share of the frames on the serial line have a wrong checksum
  State: the TX15 screen mode is MANUAL | FBWA | AUTO | RTL
    Set: let ArduPilot fly this mode
    Shows: {value}: the screen of the TX15 shows this flight mode
  State: the TX15 screen arming is armed | disarmed
    Set: arm or disarm the plane
    Shows: armed: the screen of the TX15 shows ARMED
    Shows: disarmed: the screen of the TX15 shows DISARMED
  State: the TX15 screen battery is 0..30 V
    Set: let the battery of the plane be at {value}
    Shows: {value}: the screen of the TX15 shows this battery voltage
  State: the TX15 screen bank is -90..90 degrees
    Set: bank the plane to {value}
    Shows: {value}: the screen of the TX15 shows this bank
  State: the TX15 uplink quality is 0..100 %
    Shows: {value}: the screen of the TX15 shows this uplink quality
  State: the ground station telemetry is silent | flowing
    Set: let ArduPilot send, or not send, its MAVLink telemetry
    Shows: flowing: the ground station hears the HEARTBEAT of the plane
    Shows: silent: the ground station hears nothing from the plane
  State: the ground station map distance is 0..2000 m
    Set: fly the plane this far north of home
    Shows: {value}: the plane on the map of the ground station is this far north of home
  State: the ground station command is not sent | sent
    Set: send a command to the plane from the ground station
  State: the autopilot command is not received | received
    Shows: received: ArduPilot gets the command of the ground station
  State: the ground station telemetry rate is 0..10000 bytes per second
    Shows: {value}: the telemetry that reaches the ground station in one second

Background:
  Given the TX15 is connected
  And the TX15 roll stick is 0 %
  And the TX15 pitch stick is 0 %
  And the TX15 throttle stick is 0 %
  And the TX15 arm switch is off
  And the corrupted frames are 0 %
  And the TX15 screen mode is MANUAL
  And the TX15 screen arming is disarmed
  And the TX15 screen battery is 12 V
  And the TX15 screen bank is 0 degrees
  And the ground station telemetry is silent
  And the ground station map distance is 0 m
